Summary: winemac: load plugin libraries named in WINEMAC_PLUGINS before Cocoa starts
Category: system
Kind: feature
Feature: embedding
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Note: after Second Chance's weak-dylib load command patched into
    winemac.so
Upstream: no
Why: An app that embeds Wine may need code of its own inside the Mac driver
 (Objective-C hooks on Wine's windows, say). Without a hook it has to add a
 load command to winemac.so and re-sign it. Now macdrv_init dlopens each
 path in the WINEMAC_PLUGINS environment variable (a colon-separated list,
 inherited by child processes), after reading the options and before Cocoa
 starts. Only absolute paths are loaded: a path that doesn't start with /,
 or doesn't load, is logged (err:macdrv) and skipped. With the variable
 unset nothing changes. There is no registry setting, so nothing a program
 in the prefix writes makes a plugin load in later processes. A plugin
 must be an x86_64 (or universal) Mach-O, as the driver runs under Rosetta
 2 on Apple silicon. Its constructors run on a Wine thread inside the
 driver's DllMain, with the loader lock held and Cocoa not yet started: they
 mustn't call into Wine or wait on the main thread, and AppKit work has to
 be deferred (dispatch_async to the main queue runs once Cocoa does).
Programs: Second Chance (an app that embeds Wine): had to patch a load
 command into winemac.so and re-sign it to load its in-process helpers
Enable: env WINEMAC_PLUGINS=/abs/a.dylib:/abs/b.dylib (inherited by child processes)
Messages: "plugin path %s isn't absolute; skipped", "couldn't load plugin
 %s: %s" (err:macdrv; WINEDEBUG=err-macdrv or -all hides them)
Risk: loads native code (dlopen, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL) into every Wine
 process that starts the Mac driver, from the paths in WINEMAC_PLUGINS.
 Whoever sets the environment Wine starts in turns it on, and child
 processes inherit it. Unsigned plugins load (Wine isn't hardened-runtime).
Uncertain: a plugin that needs to run before the Mac Driver options are
 read, or after Cocoa has started, isn't served by this point; none known.
Related: winemac-cocoa-start-wait, winemac-activation-policy; they also
 change setup_options and macdrv_init
Status: 11.22: 2026-11-26: the Plugins registry value dropped and relative
 paths refused (review decision 21); not yet in a build. The earlier form
 (variable and registry value) passed winemac-plugins in 11.22-build9, and
 Second Chance loaded its helpers through it on meeka (macOS 26.7).

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
index db14f64..591042a 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/macdrv_main.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "macdrv.h"
 
+#include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <Security/AuthSession.h>
 #include <IOKit/pwr_mgt/IOPMLib.h>
 
@@ -423,6 +424,36 @@ static void load_strings(struct localized_string *str)
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *              load_plugins
+ *
+ * dlopen each path in WINEMAC_PLUGINS (inherited by child processes), a
+ * colon-separated list of absolute paths, before Cocoa starts. Lets an app
+ * that embeds Wine add code to the driver without changing winemac.so. A
+ * path that isn't absolute, or doesn't load, is reported and skipped.
+ * Nothing is loaded unless the variable is set.
+ */
+static void load_plugins(void)
+{
+    const char *list = getenv("WINEMAC_PLUGINS");
+    char *copy, *path, *next;
+
+    if (!list || !*list || !(copy = strdup(list))) return;
+    for (path = copy; path; path = next)
+    {
+        if ((next = strchr(path, ':'))) *next++ = 0;
+        if (!*path) continue;
+        if (path[0] != '/')
+            ERR("plugin path %s isn't absolute; skipped\n", debugstr_a(path));
+        else if (dlopen(path, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_GLOBAL))
+            TRACE("loaded plugin %s\n", debugstr_a(path));
+        else
+            ERR("couldn't load plugin %s: %s\n", debugstr_a(path), dlerror());
+    }
+    free(copy);
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *              macdrv_init
  */
@@ -446,6 +477,7 @@ static NTSTATUS macdrv_init(void *arg)
 
     init_win_context();
     setup_options();
+    load_plugins();
     load_strings(params->strings);
 
     if (macdrv_start_cocoa_app(NtGetTickCount()))
